{
 "about": "Scroll band at the top of the tall panel of the left door leaf of the Garden Gate (plate 4, 'North Side of Garden Gate'), left half, drawn by hand as smooth curves while viewing the University of Manchester copy of the 1786 engravings online (PR-CHCR-00457, image 26). Only these hand-drawn control points are used; no pixels of that scan. Coordinates are that scan's pixels. Curves are Catmull-Rom splines through the points; polylines are straight. The right half is the mirror image; the engraver drew the five-petal rosette slightly turned, it is drawn here upright (one petal pointing down). The raised border runs out to the panel's top and side, so the ground is only the marked pockets.",
